The '''1996 UEFA Champions League final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match played on 22 May 1996 between title holders [[AFC Ajax|Ajax]] of the Netherlands and [[Juventus FC|Juventus]] of Italy. The match ended in a 1–1 draw after extra time, forcing a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]], which Juventus won 4–2.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/european/ajax-juventus-1996-champions-league-final-doping-cheating-calciopoli-a8860746.html|title=Why Ajax still feel 'cheated' by Juve's 1996 Champions League triumph|date=9 April 2019|website=The Independent}}</ref> It was the club's second and most recent triumph in the competition. As of 2026, this is the last time a Dutch team appeared in a Champions League final.

==Background==
The match was a repeat of the [[1973 European Cup final|1973]] final, making it the fourth repeated final pairing.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefachampionsleague/news/0245-0e98c715cad7-29a5fa4a1a1b-1000--second-time-round-european-cup-final-rematches/ |title=Second time round: European Cup final rematches |publisher=UEFA|date=16 May 2017}}</ref> Ajax won the 1973 final 1–0. Ajax was defending the title, having won in [[1995 UEFA Champions League final|1995]] when they defeated [[AC Milan|Milan]] 1–0.

Juventus had not featured in the Champions League for nine years until this edition of the tournament. Juventus reached their fourth final. In the semi-finals, Juventus eliminated French side Nantes, with a 2-0 victory in the first leg at home, and 3–2 defeat in the return leg. Previously Juventus won the final in [[1985 European Cup final|1985]], and lost in [[1973 European Cup final|1973]] and [[1983 European Cup final|1983]].

Ajax reached their sixth final. In the semi-finals, Ajax eliminated Greek side [[Panathinaikos F.C.|Panathinaikos]]; they lost the first leg 1–0 at home, but won 3–0 in the second leg. Previously Ajax won the finals in [[1971 European Cup final|1971]], [[1972 European Cup final|1972]], [[1973 European Cup final|1973]] and [[1995 UEFA Champions League final|1995]], and lost in [[1969 European Cup final|1969]].

Juventus entered the final as [[1995–96 Serie A]] runners-up to Milan, as well as [[1995 Supercoppa Italiana]] winners. Ajax entered the final as [[1995–96 Eredivisie]] champions, [[1995 Dutch Supercup]] winners, [[1995 UEFA Super Cup]] and [[1995 Intercontinental Cup]] winners.

